{"kind":"assert","text":"Review observations for retired exact86f8f692 (not an effective review verdict; primary a75c4096 retired while filing). Changes requested for exact 86f8f6926ffb158743879bfda25fda869266aad7, sole primary a75c4096 (notes/2026-10-15-hosted-counter-contracts.md). Design review only.\n\nF1 P2 — make the declared utterance rule enforce the promised numeral boundary (lines 63–68, 309–312). A direct probe of the pinned evaluator returned true for n=3 with utterance \"13\" and \"x3x\", as well as \"3\" and \"number 3\". Concatenation \u0026 works, but $contains is substring matching. The host whole-token filter does not protect generic native say submissions. Define the intended boundary exactly and enforce it in the declared definition using supported bounded expressions, or choose a simpler native representation whose checked field actually guarantees the intended output. Witness native say admissions/refusals for exact numeral, embedded digits, embedded letters, punctuation and Unicode; use the same semantics at the host boundary.\n\nF2 P2 — retain a durable way to observe resume (lines 278–284, 328). When every role is paused the alarm is disabled. The only remaining observer is a finite read session/stream; a restart closes that stream. A later resume-role is an ordinary team-scope act, and agent-team declares no sends, so that act need not invoke AgentTeam. After stream loss there is no specified event that recreates the observer. Keep bounded control catch-up while attached and paused, or define an equally durable authorized wake protocol for every relevant control. Cover pause-all, stream expiry/object eviction, then resume through generic MCP with no browser or host-status request; eligible work must resume. Also cover initially zero live rows followed by first setup/control.\n\nF3 P2 — replace the asserted universal input-cost bound with a model admission contract (lines 201–238). inputBytes+256 is not yet justified for any selected model's actual chat framing/tokenization; a messages/usage smoke test does not prove an upper bound. Missing usage and restart charging depend on this being an upper bound. Require each catalog entry to retain a defensible bound for the complete provider input, including framing/special tokens and any charged token categories, plus an enforced output bound; unsupported models remain unavailable. Define settlement for malformed usage or reported cost above the reservation (preserve charges, fence subsequent calls, no silent clamp/release). A finite model-specific maximum can be simpler than a tokenizer claim. Witness limits, absent/invalid usage, and above-bound reports. Selecting models/default allowance remains Hugh's decision; this requests the admission rule, not that selection now. Cloudflare publishes model-specific token/Neuron rates: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/ ; its binding contract: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/configuration/bindings/ . Neither establishes this note's fixed 256 framing allowance.\n\nArchitecture — the separate declared team scope plus one exact host attachment is a reasonable settings owner; settings need not move into Counter. Preserve full Counter/team ScopeRefs including incarnation and verify declared-definition/factory affiliation at attachment, rather than trusting the app field alone. One custody/ledger/assignment object is the useful simplification. F2 is the missing recovery edge.\n\nSecurity — retaining model output as data, no bearer/signing route/tools, separate administer/configure grants and controller checks are sound boundaries. The intended native output invariant and reservation bound still require F1/F3. Status read access by live agents.configure or agents.administer is consistent with the stated admin-only initial configuration policy; it need not be public. The new control domain must retain the existing signed-envelope operation/subject/body/deadline binding, not merely a standing check.\n\nSimplification — keep one native utterance validation rule and one host owner. Keep model-specific admissibility and cost assumptions in the catalog. Do not add a harness, sandbox or another identity mechanism to solve these findings.\n\nAnswers to explicit checker questions: \u0026 produces the numeral string, but $contains fails the whole-token requirement (F1). A focused applicationValues probe with declared scope field accepted and preserved a full lane ScopeRef and injected the trusted opener; this proves typed genesis transport, not scope creation or authority affiliation. The new definitions still need their proposed in-memory judgments. The universal byte/framing bound is unproven (F3). Status-role answer is above.\n\nNonblocking contract clarifications for the next draft: (a) The parent explicitly permits an administrative ceiling reduction below spent/reserved usage as a prospective fence. State whether set-allocation may similarly lower a role below its historical charges, and show used/reserved/remaining without erasing charges or implying that history was freed. Test generic scope control plus concurrent reservation. (b) Reservation precedes commit while its ID names a promise: specify a stable provisional identity and binding to the admitted promise, including the already owed commit/assignment crash witness. (c) Treat abort/timeout as local cancellation unless provider completion is proved; retain unresolved cost and distinguish one active local dispatch from possible still-running provider work after a timeout/restart. The reviewed documentation does not establish physical provider cancellation by env.AI.run(...,{signal}).\n\nValidation: exact note and parent sections read; relevant native definition/evaluator/factory/session/custody boundaries inspected; pure evaluator and typed-genesis probes run. No source edits, gate rerun, live provider call, GitHub push or Cloudflare deployment. Hugh's written-output/UI/model/default/lost-reply